## RAG-Based Semantic Search (aisearch/)

A **RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation)** search layer built on top of Elasticsearch, enabling hybrid search (keyword + semantic) across both structured PLM data and unstructured PDF documents, with LLM-generated answers.

### Environment Verified

Before designing the system, the following components were tested and confirmed working:

| Component | What Was Checked | Result |
|---|---|---|
| **Elasticsearch** | Local install (e.g. `C:\ramesh2026\apps\elasticsearch` on Windows or `/opt/elasticsearch` on Linux) | Version **9.4.2** — supports inference pipelines and `dense_vector` (RRF done in Python — ES built-in RRF requires a Platinum license) |
| **Embedding API** | `POST /v1/embeddings` with model `bge-m3` | Working — returns **1024-dimension** vectors; OpenAI-compatible format |
| **Chat API** | `POST /v1/chat/completions` with model `deepseek-v4-flash` | Working — OpenAI-compatible format; used for RAG answer generation |
| **Reranker API** | Available model `qwen3-reranker-0.6b` | Supported — can optionally improve result ranking |
| **PDF sources** | `data/volume/` directory | **135 PDF spec sheets** for parts |
| **Structured data** | `db/bicycle_plm.db` (SQLite) | 7 tables with parts, BOM, costing, ECO, AML, AVL, CAD |

### How It Works — Architecture Overview

```
User enters query ("find brake assembly costs")
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│  Query Embedding  │  Python calls Siemens API to embed the query
│  (via llm_client)  │  Uses model: bge-m3 → 1024-dim vector
└────────┬─────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      Python Hybrid Search Engine          │
│                                            │
│  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐│
│  │  ES BM25 query   │  │  ES kNN query    ││
│  │  (keyword match) │  │  (vector search) ││
│  └────────┬────────┘  └────────┬────────┘│
│           │                    │           │
│           └────── RRF ────────┘           │
│           (Python Reciprocal Rank Fusion)  │
│                      │                     │
│                Top 10 results              │
└──────────────────────┬─────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│   RAG Engine      │  Build context from results
│                   │  Call deepseek-v4-flash:
│  context + query  │  → generates answer with citations
│  ──────────────▶  │
│  answer + cites   │
└─────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│   Search UI       │  Show: LLM answer at top, results below
│                   │  Filter by entity type, paginate results
└─────────────────┘
```

### Component Details

#### Why This Architecture (ES Inference Pipeline Approach)

Elasticsearch 9.4.2 can call the Siemens LLM API **internally** to generate embeddings — no Python code is needed for embedding computation. This means:

- **Indexing**: Python reads data (SQLite rows, PDF text) and pushes raw JSON documents to ES. ES's ingest pipeline automatically calls `bge-m3` to generate the 1024-dim vector and stores it alongside the text.
- **Searching**: Python embeds the query via `llm_client`, then runs BM25 and kNN as separate ES queries. Results are fused via Python's `_rrf_fusion()` (RRF formula: `1/(k+rank)`). This avoids ES's built-in RRF which requires a Platinum license.
- **RAG**: Python only needs to call the chat API (`deepseek-v4-flash`) for answer generation — the retrieval is fully handled by ES.

#### Elasticsearch Indices (8 total)

Each PLM entity gets its own ES index with:
- **Text fields** (`text` type) — enables BM25 keyword search (e.g., searching for "brake" matches part names, descriptions)
- **Vector field** (`dense_vector`, 1024 dims) — enables semantic search (e.g., finding "stopping mechanism" parts even if they don't contain the word "brake")
- **Keyword fields** (`keyword` type) — enables exact filtering (e.g., filter by status="RELEASED" or entity type)
- **Ingest pipeline** — auto-generates the vector from combined text fields during indexing

| Index | Source | Content Indexed | Why It Helps Search |
|---|---|---|---|
| `plm_parts` | SQLite `parts` table | part_number, part_name, material, spec_file, status | Find parts by name, material, or specification |
| `plm_bom` | SQLite `bom` table | part_number, part_name, parent_assembly, bom_type | Trace assembly hierarchies and find where a part is used |
| `plm_costing` | SQLite `costing_bom` table | part_number, part_name, cost_type, costs | Find cost data for assemblies |
| `plm_eco` | SQLite `engineering_change_orders` table | eco_number, eco_title, description, change_detail | Search engineering changes affecting a part |
| `plm_aml` | SQLite `approved_manufacturer_list` table | part_number, manufacturer_name, mpn | Find who makes a part |
| `plm_avl` | SQLite `approved_vendor_list` table | part_number, vendor_name, vpn | Find who supplies a part |
| `plm_cad` | SQLite `cad_metadata` table | part_number, cad_file_name, drawing_number | Find CAD files for a part |
| `plm_docs` | `data/volume/*.pdf` | Extracted text per page/chunk with source filename | Full-text search across 135 PDF spec sheets |

#### Hybrid Search (BM25 + Vector + RRF)

| Search Method | What It Does | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **BM25 (keyword)** | Matches exact terms in text fields — the traditional "search engine" approach | Searching "aluminum frame" finds parts with those exact words in their description |
| **kNN (vector/semantic)** | Matches by meaning, not exact words — finds conceptually similar content even with different terminology | Searching "lightweight structure" finds "aluminum frame" parts even though the words don't match |
| **RRF fusion** | Combines both result lists into a single ranked list using Python's `_rrf_fusion()` — the RRF formula `1/(60+rank)` runs in Python on retrieved hits | Parts that rank well in BOTH methods appear at the top |

#### RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation)

The RAG flow:
1. **User query** enters the search bar
2. **Hybrid search** retrieves the top 10 most relevant documents (from any entity type)
3. **Context building** — the content of those 10 results is assembled into a structured context
4. **LLM generation** — the query + context is sent to `deepseek-v4-flash` with a prompt that asks it to answer based only on the provided context
5. **Answer + citations** — the LLM response is displayed at the top of the search page, with numbered citations linking to the source results below

Example:
```
Q: "What is the cost of the brake assembly?"

A: The brake assembly (BRK-001) has a total rolled cost of $18.75,
   consisting of:
   - Brake Lever Set (BRK-002): $8.50 (material $3.00, labor $2.50)
   - Brake Caliper (BRK-003): $6.25 (material $2.00, labor $1.75)
   [1] BIKE-001 Costing BOM  [2] BRK-001 Part Detail
```

### Directory Structure

```
aisearch/                        # All RAG search artifacts
├── .env                         # LLM_API_KEY (gitignored)
├── config.py                    # ES host, LLM URL, model names, index list
├── es_client.py                 # ES connection + index creation with mappings
├── llm_client.py                # Embedding + chat API client
├── setup_es.py                  # One-time: create inference endpoint + pipelines
│
├── index_builders/              # Python scripts to populate ES indices
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── base.py                  # Shared base: read SQLAlchemy → push to ES
│   ├── build_parts.py           # Index parts table
│   ├── build_bom.py             # Index BOM table
│   ├── build_costing.py         # Index costing table
│   ├── build_eco.py             # Index ECO table
│   ├── build_aml.py             # Index AML table
│   ├── build_avl.py             # Index AVL table
│   ├── build_cad.py             # Index CAD table
│   ├── build_docs.py            # Parse PDFs → chunk → index
│   └── build_all.py             # Run all builders sequentially
│
├── search.py                    # hybrid_search(): BM25 + knn + RRF
├── rag.py                       # rag_answer(): search → context → LLM → answer
│                                # rag_answer_multimodal(): search + vision LLM → answer
├── vision.py                    # Multimodal vision module — prepare_image() + vision_chat()
├── router.py                    # FastAPI routes for search UI + /search/multimodal
├── templates/
│   └── search.html              # RAG search page (extends base.html)
│
├── start_es.bat                 # Start Elasticsearch
├── build_indices.bat            # Build/search indices from scratch
└── rebuild_indices.bat          # Drop + recreate + rebuild
```

### Running the RAG Search

| Step | Command | What It Does |
|---|---|---|
| Start ES | `./start_es.sh` (Linux/macOS) or `start_es.bat` (Windows) — launches ES on localhost:9200 |
| Setup inference | `python -m aisearch.setup_es` | Creates ES inference endpoint, ingest pipelines and index mappings |
| Build indices | `python -m aisearch.index_builders.build_all` | Reads SQLite + PDFs, pushes to ES (ES auto-embeds via pipeline) |
| Start app | `python -m app.main` | Web UI on localhost:8000 with search at /search |
| Full startup | `./rebuild_indices.sh` (Linux/macOS) or `rebuild_indices.bat` (Windows) | Drops old indices, rebuilds fresh, starts server |

### How Each Component Helps the User Search

| Component | User Benefit |
|---|---|
| **BM25 keyword search** | Exact matches for known part numbers, ECO numbers, manufacturer names — like searching "BRK-001" finds the brake part immediately |
| **Vector semantic search** | Conceptual matches — searching "stopping mechanism" finds brake-related parts even though the term "stopping" never appears in the data |
| **RRF fusion** | No need to guess whether to use keywords or natural language — both work simultaneously and the best results surface |
| **Entity-type filter** | Narrow results to specific domains — parts only, ECOs only, documents only |
| **RAG answer generation** | Get a synthesized answer with citations instead of clicking through multiple pages. Ask "what changed in the brake assembly last quarter?" and get a summary with ECO references |
| **PDF content search** | Search inside 135 spec sheet PDFs without opening each one — the text is chunked, embedded, and indexed by page |
| **Unified search across all data** | One search bar searches parts, BOM, costing, ECOs, manufacturers, vendors, CAD files, and PDF documents simultaneously |

---

## Implementation Summary

The RAG search system was implemented as the `aisearch/` package using **Approach B**: Elasticsearch handles embedding internally via its inference pipeline. The Siemens LLM API is only called directly for RAG answer generation (chat) and as a fallback for query embedding.

### Implementation Phases

| Phase | What Was Built | Key Files |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Core Infrastructure** | Config, ES connection, LLM API client | [config.py](aisearch/config.py), [es_client.py](aisearch/es_client.py), [llm_client.py](aisearch/llm_client.py), [setup_es.py](aisearch/setup_es.py) |
| **2. Index Builders** | 8 entity-specific builders + base class | [index_builders/](aisearch/index_builders/) (11 files) |
| **3. Search Engine** | Hybrid BM25 + vector + RRF search | [search.py](aisearch/search.py) |
| **4. RAG Engine** | Retrieve → context → LLM → answer | [rag.py](aisearch/rag.py) |
| **5. UI + API** | SSR search page + JSON API endpoint | [router.py](aisearch/router.py), [search.html](aisearch/templates/search.html) |
| **6. Batch Files** | Startup and index-building with prereq checks | [start_es.bat](aisearch/start_es.bat), [build_indices.bat](aisearch/build_indices.bat), [rebuild_indices.bat](aisearch/rebuild_indices.bat) |
| **7. Vision Module** | Multimodal image processing + vision LLM client | [vision.py](aisearch/vision.py) |

### Design Decisions

1. **ES inference pipeline for embeddings**: ES 9.4.2 natively supports calling external APIs for vector generation. During indexing, raw JSON documents are pushed to ES, and the ingest pipeline (`plm-auto-embed`) automatically calls `bge-m3` via Siemens API and stores the 1024-dim vector in `content_vector`. During search, ES auto-embeds the user query the same way — no Python-side embedding needed.

2. **Hybrid search with Python RRF**: Each query runs BM25 and kNN as separate ES queries (no special license needed). Results are fused in Python via `_rrf_fusion()` using the Reciprocal Rank Fusion formula `1/(60+rank)` — giving the same balanced relevance as ES built-in RRF but without requiring a Platinum license.

3. **SSR-first UI**: The search page follows the same pattern as the existing app — server-side rendered Jinja2 template extending `base.html`, with form-based filtering and pagination. A `/search/api` JSON endpoint is also provided for programmatic access.

4. **Detailed telemetry**: Both search and RAG responses include a `timing` breakdown (total, embed, search, retrieve, LLM seconds) exposed in the UI's collapsible "Search Telemetry" panel for debugging and observability.

---

## Multimodal Vision Module (aisearch/vision.py)

A reusable vision module that processes images and sends them alongside text to any OpenAI-compatible vision LLM. Adapted from the drawing-interpreter tool at `drawing-interpreter/drawing_interpreter.py` (adjacent in the repo).

### Image Preparation — `prepare_image()`

```python
from aisearch.vision import prepare_image

# Given raw bytes and a filename, returns a prepared image dict
prepared = prepare_image(raw, filename="drawing.png")
# → { "filename": "drawing.png", "mime_type": "image/png",
#     "base64_data": "data:image/png;base64,iVBOR...",
#     "size_bytes": 789699, "size_display": "771.2 KB" }
```

- Validates the image (Pillow), returns `ImageValidationError` for corrupt/unrecognized files
- Downscales images larger than `VISION_MAX_IMAGE_DIMENSION` (default 4096px) using LANCZOS resampling
- Re-encodes non-native API formats (BMP, TIFF) to PNG; keeps JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP unchanged when small enough
- Returns base64 data URI ready for `{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": prepared["base64_data"]}}`

### Vision LLM Call — `vision_chat()`

```python
from aisearch.vision import vision_chat

reply = vision_chat(
    system_prompt="You are a PLM assistant.",
    user_message="What part does this drawing show?",
    images=[prepared],  # list of dicts from prepare_image()
    model=VISION_MODEL,  # defaults to VISION_MODEL, then CHAT_MODEL
    max_tokens=4096,
)
# → "This is an engineering drawing of a brake caliper..."
```

- Sync client (matches existing FastAPI route handler pattern)
- Uses the OpenAI SDK (`openai.OpenAI`) pointed at `LLM_BASE_URL` / `LLM_API_KEY`
- Retries transient errors (connection errors, 429, 5xx) with exponential backoff (`MAX_RETRIES=4`, base 2s)
- Raises `VisionAPIError` if all retries exhausted or the model rejects the request

### Exports

Functions are re-exported from `aisearch.llm_client` so consumers can import from one place:

```python
from aisearch.llm_client import vision_chat, prepare_image
```

### Integration Points

| Module | How It Consumes Vision | What Happens When Images Are Present |
|---|---|---|
| [aisearch/chat_router.py](aisearch/chat_router.py) | `POST /chat` with `files` param | Uses `prepare_image()` for upload processing; calls `vision_chat()` directly instead of the tool-calling loop |
| [aisearch/rag.py](aisearch/rag.py) | `rag_answer_multimodal()` | Retrieves context via hybrid search, then sends context + images to vision LLM. Returns `{"multimodal": true}` in result dict |
| [aisearch/router.py](aisearch/router.py) | `POST /search/multimodal` | Accepts text query + image file uploads, processes images, delegates to `rag_answer_multimodal()` |

### Configuration

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `VISION_MODEL` | `CHAT_MODEL` fallback | Model id for vision-capable LLM (e.g. `qwen/qwen3-vl-30b-a3b-instruct`) |
| `VISION_MAX_IMAGE_DIMENSION` | `4096` | Longest side in px; larger images are downscaled |
| `VISION_MAX_TOKENS` | `4096` | Max tokens in the vision LLM response |
| `VISION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `180` | Per-request timeout in seconds |

### Design Decisions

1. **OpenAI SDK over raw `requests`**: The `openai` library handles multipart content arrays, streaming, and retry semantics natively. The existing `llm_client.py` uses `requests` for chat/embed; `vision.py` uses the SDK because OpenRouter's multimodal endpoint works more reliably through it.
2. **Sync not async**: FastAPI route handlers in this project are sync (no `async def` used elsewhere in `aisearch/`). Using a sync `OpenAI()` client avoids mixing sync/async paradigms.
3. **Configurable model**: `VISION_MODEL` can differ from `CHAT_MODEL` — vision models are often different (e.g. `qwen/qwen3-vl-30b-a3b-instruct` vs `google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite`).
4. **Graceful fallback in chat_router**: If `prepare_image()` raises an exception (e.g. Pillow can't decode the file), the chat router falls back to a simple raw base64 encode so the user still gets a response.

### Verifications Performed

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| ES 9.4.2 local install | Confirmed — supports inference pipelines and dense_vector (RRF done in Python) |
| Siemens embeddings API (bge-m3) | Working — returns 1024-dim vectors, OpenAI-compatible format |
| Siemens chat API (deepseek-v4-flash) | Working — OpenAI-compatible format |
| All Python imports resolve | Verified |
| Search template renders (empty + results) | Verified |
| App starts with all routes | Verified — 18 routes registered including /search and /search/api |

### Existing File Changes

The following existing files were modified to integrate the RAG search system:

| File | Change | Why |
|---|---|---|
| [app/main.py](app/main.py) | Added `aisearch.router` import and `app.include_router()` | Registers the `/search` and `/search/api` routes in the FastAPI app |
| [app/template_utils.py](app/template_utils.py) | Added `aisearch/templates/` to the Jinja2 `FileSystemLoader` search paths | Allows the search template (`search.html`) to extend `base.html` and be rendered alongside app templates |
| [app/templates/base.html](app/templates/base.html) | Added "Search" link in sidebar nav with `<hr>` divider | Provides navigation to the search page from all other pages |
| [requirements.txt](requirements.txt) | Added `elasticsearch`, `pypdf`, `requests`, `python-dotenv` | Required dependencies for ES connectivity, PDF parsing, LLM API calls, and .env file loading |
| [.gitignore](.gitignore) | Added `aisearch/.env`, `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`, `.env` | Prevents API keys and Python cache files from being committed to version control |
| [aisearch/vision.py](aisearch/vision.py) | **New** — modular image processing + vision LLM client | Provides `prepare_image()` and `vision_chat()` for multimodal support across chat and search |
| [aisearch/config.py](aisearch/config.py) | Added `VISION_MODEL`, `VISION_MAX_IMAGE_DIMENSION`, `VISION_MAX_TOKENS`, `VISION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | Config for vision-capable model, separate from text-only `CHAT_MODEL` |
| [aisearch/llm_client.py](aisearch/llm_client.py) | Added re-exports: `from aisearch.vision import vision_chat, prepare_image` | Lets consumers import everything from `llm_client` |
| [aisearch/chat_router.py](aisearch/chat_router.py) | Image upload→`prepare_image()`, vision path→`vision_chat()` | Images are properly resized/encoded; sends vision LLM calls through OpenAI SDK |
| [aisearch/rag.py](aisearch/rag.py) | Added `rag_answer_multimodal()` with shared helpers | Search context + images sent to vision LLM; returns `{"multimodal": true}` |
| [aisearch/router.py](aisearch/router.py) | Added `POST /search/multimodal` | Accepts text + image uploads for multimodal RAG search |
| [aisearch/templates/search.html](aisearch/templates/search.html) | Collapsible "Image Search" upload panel | Users can upload drawings alongside text queries |
| [requirements.txt](requirements.txt) | Added `openai>=1.50.0`, `Pillow>=10.0.0` | New dependencies for OpenAI SDK-based vision calls and image processing |

